[{:db/id "q-348849/field-1/fea7f6b22e69e29a9716f674d580a63eca4b26e1b4ae5c4f38b3026c28b2b97d" :answer/id #uuid "bf80b704-2d1d-5182-ac36-f6dacc958325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348849/field-1/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf" :answer/id #uuid "e9c3b835-2fb6-5a86-9974-38ca46832f76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348849/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "97a30074-00e7-5cfa-bf12-ea4dac172a56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348849/field-1/fea7f6b22e69e29a9716f674d580a63eca4b26e1b4ae5c4f38b3026c28b2b97d" :answer-field/choices ["q-348849/field-1/fea7f6b22e69e29a9716f674d580a63eca4b26e1b4ae5c4f38b3026c28b2b97d" "q-348849/field-1/1a9483841df301d0d8304986bfec9a52b4f49d31cfd2980ff1d8d6f175662caf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348849" :question/id #uuid "96b50352-18f5-5bbb-a700-23a71998ea44" :question/math-academy-id "q-348849" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{8x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{8x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{8})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{8})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{8} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{3}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{3}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{3}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348849/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df0c3b59-7667-53e9-84d3-bba30ea116fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348618/field-1/69f68537d5874fa3d218994e824956ca38c5a8c29f4335110bfcb2bf893e4477" :answer/id #uuid "d7be36c3-2e63-5e50-a917-21fa8a0fb77b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{243}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348618/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd436f7-c07c-5fa8-94c9-33dcb2ea1853" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348618/field-1/69f68537d5874fa3d218994e824956ca38c5a8c29f4335110bfcb2bf893e4477" :answer-field/choices ["q-348618/field-1/69f68537d5874fa3d218994e824956ca38c5a8c29f4335110bfcb2bf893e4477"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348618" :question/id #uuid "1d787e1b-6005-525c-b60a-10567e5eaf1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-348618" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{5}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{5}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I \\\\ 6I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{6}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{6}-{0}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{243}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348618/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df0c3b59-7667-53e9-84d3-bba30ea116fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348618"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999/selection/09f9568b9032a258744b73b08553a45679ce3baf10e1847349ddb9cf78a3d261" :answer/id #uuid "44ce7db0-39c3-5ce8-8b58-c2b7add9cd94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999/selection/830a08a17a3bc68a8e849c8d7e7a7e21cd8b84724f1767acc4bccbeebb91b0c8" :answer/id #uuid "19059a79-9956-586b-918e-1018529a7bc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "3e3224dc-2808-536b-b49a-49ac7dd24874" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "4f60f33c-c465-51e4-a10c-671d2066ab02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999/selection/ba44b4fbcaae846ba4309a542376e83c513c18bae11806aa24ae75ceb4042ae5" :answer/id #uuid "1f70ba3f-d391-5ae8-be76-9db025504ba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f97fdf9-0efc-5c35-87ec-c19ec5c7fc0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114999/selection/ba44b4fbcaae846ba4309a542376e83c513c18bae11806aa24ae75ceb4042ae5" :answer-field/choices ["q-114999/selection/09f9568b9032a258744b73b08553a45679ce3baf10e1847349ddb9cf78a3d261" "q-114999/selection/830a08a17a3bc68a8e849c8d7e7a7e21cd8b84724f1767acc4bccbeebb91b0c8" "q-114999/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-114999/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" "q-114999/selection/ba44b4fbcaae846ba4309a542376e83c513c18bae11806aa24ae75ceb4042ae5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114999" :question/id #uuid "5aca29c8-5475-59ea-8c66-9b60c30722ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-114999" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{9}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{9}⁡x)(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{9{ln}^{8}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9\\int \\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4}-9I \\\\ 10I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{10}⁡x}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{9}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡x){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}({ln}^{10}⁡(e)-{ln}^{10}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df0c3b59-7667-53e9-84d3-bba30ea116fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114999"] :db/ensure [:kno