stion/math-academy-id "q-114952" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts." :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nI=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{2}⁡x(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4}-2I \\\\ 3I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{12}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114952/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df0c3b59-7667-53e9-84d3-bba30ea116fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114952"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609/selection/020803676f5c1c01a1fd397d4727fa1736773ba4465c800ed9f5c1cc9096e1d8" :answer/id #uuid "210e166e-60ee-5c66-93fc-2a2a1f067bed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609/selection/c26cb46b66a05ee89a4e92205485c2a80b770c41977430509b094707c5be46bd" :answer/id #uuid "ca9b0efe-3d56-5862-a13d-99b4e8b336a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609/selection/2aa1a1f03e6635c235d028360fefbc76d754f21df176a1ef790502d852a71c09" :answer/id #uuid "f106a948-5ba6-5ac5-bdd9-7b320ff4d9a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609/selection/789a429f1a6b990fb760129cca867a9560075f5255823f52bb855141d18282e0" :answer/id #uuid "077d3f97-da7c-50e7-abe2-d81ac948568f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609/selection/6299b8dd2be42dc16e3fafd6ef190d7eea310b9146d340903bd51aa688ff6f5f" :answer/id #uuid "a2f4d064-7e6c-5231-b016-de9ade2872fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e01866d-e3fa-546d-a8a6-b2409a025a36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49609/selection/c26cb46b66a05ee89a4e92205485c2a80b770c41977430509b094707c5be46bd" :answer-field/choices ["q-49609/selection/020803676f5c1c01a1fd397d4727fa1736773ba4465c800ed9f5c1cc9096e1d8" "q-49609/selection/c26cb46b66a05ee89a4e92205485c2a80b770c41977430509b094707c5be46bd" "q-49609/selection/2aa1a1f03e6635c235d028360fefbc76d754f21df176a1ef790502d852a71c09" "q-49609/selection/789a429f1a6b990fb760129cca867a9560075f5255823f52bb855141d18282e0" "q-49609/selection/6299b8dd2be42dc16e3fafd6ef190d7eea310b9146d340903bd51aa688ff6f5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49609" :question/id #uuid "3f752a5a-deed-56d6-992b-90e858e58c9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49609" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2J \\\\ I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2(-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4I \\\\ 5I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49609/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b428331b-4916-5b2c-8aa6-89a2358cdef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409/selection/29e01902db3cef67892592ec997db0536bcd056471e9c0d7ae874c01f9562ac9" :answer/id #uuid "490f37fe-3aca-59cf-b01d-ff2ddc1c387c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409/selection/c5dbaa181badcf3675003330e14ea3d99947791d0dcea710d1a50671d93375b7" :answer/id #uuid "1ef47da1-b52c-5e48-9d99-d8ad05f189dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409/selection/62a578485c803f42aaae460e285de07f578ef3aa0d0c7af8f57ba00ce71d69f4" :answer/id #uuid "a5fe1e70-4ad6-5066-be68-cde45d36d26d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{3}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409/selection/76e8305cd40ec618b73f6ee234ee60e512a280e380b654fdb85a5f9c64f12eb1" :answer/id #uuid "0cf0e015-4593-5067-a937-4d1e248dfb73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409/selection/49589add2d5e28670680444510c3a8e2c0849dda3553009f67527044e0f0b92e" :answer/id #uuid "bad78a0e-8ca6-5121-93ea-dd0fcbfb432e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f314f5-f770-5b71-bc5f-18b0a68b5b18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15409/selection/c5dbaa181badcf3675003330e14ea3d99947791d0dcea710d1a50671d93375b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-15409/selection/29e01902db3cef67892592ec997db0536bcd056471e9c0d7ae874c01f9562ac9" "q-15409/selection/c5dbaa181badcf3675003330e14ea3d99947791d0dcea710d1a50671d93375b7" "q-15409/selection/62a578485c803f42aaae460e285de07f578ef3aa0d0c7af8f57ba00ce71d69f4" "q-15409/selection/76e8305cd40ec618b73f6ee234ee60e512a280e380b654fdb85a5f9c64f12eb1" "q-15409/selection/49589add2d5e28670680444510c3a8e2c0849dda3553009f67527044e0f0b92e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15409" :question/id #uuid "4cd3af2f-abf3-5cb0-ad69-153d9969ceaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-15409" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2I) \\\\ I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4I \\\\ 5I & =-{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{5}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-15409/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b428331b-4916-5b2c-8aa6-89a2358cdef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421/selection/8ae6f6338e7f32cc759a32c74f1a03644e0be18bb8c1654a2136d5ccfd27d8b6" :answer/id #uuid "3d58f10f-2331-56a2-80af-737e14af4ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "37\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421/selection/7e68fd373637a9bca8e84b05b4351f4b39616c7d76ade5ebe308df235547c6af" :answer/id #uuid "cd0c5f0f-dd21-594b-9278-cab6f9b005d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{37}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421/selection/675b1faa963c6a3619c7aa67f80508809d5b9257dcb7efbffc63d1b3479b0a68" :answer/id #uuid "515d424d-f021-58a0-8d23-43b60f11395e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421/selection/589765f6a941d3aa2891dd1213202c0577205ee0b8910dbda61f68bd61a6e74d" :answer/id #uuid "407a1e16-433d-5cd8-a662-30556351fb89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{7}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421/selection/2dd6dc632884e05b860caf89e753846402f889fd76a6d785e826f4a2eddff4e2" :answer/id #uuid "b4992c51-9308-526a-a554-01e4225bb6b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d5ab2f-2bd0-5928-8590-ee841f54ef4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15421/selection/7e68fd373637a9bca8e84b05b4351f4b39616c7d76ade5ebe308df235547c6af" :answer-field/choices ["q-15421/selection/8ae6f6338e7f32cc759a32c74f1a03644e0be18bb8c1654a2136d5ccfd27d8b6" "q-15421/selection/7e68fd373637a9bca8e84b05b4351f4b39616c7d76ade5ebe308df235547c6af" "q-15421/selection/675b1faa963c6a3619c7aa67f80508809d5b9257dcb7efbffc63d1b3479b0a68" "q-15421/selection/589765f6a941d3aa2891dd1213202c0577205ee0b8910dbda61f68bd61a6e74d" "q-15421/selection/2dd6dc632884e05b860caf89e753846402f889fd76a6d785e826f4a2eddff4e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15421" :question/id #uuid "83d98efe-1ed1-5349-93e2-811fc076fc47" :question/math-academy-id "q-15421" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{6x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6{e}^{6x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(6{e}^{6x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{6x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6{e}^{6x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(6{e}^{6x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\int {e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6({e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6I) \\\\ I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-36I \\\\ 37I & =-{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+6{e}^{6x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{37}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15421/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b428331b-4916-5b2c-8aa6-89a2358cdef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919/selection/0f1b11f7d6616c0d1a0bcd0f9424e89602dea70c09ef29602c8cca57bf190eda" :answer/id #uuid "0bdafcfc-429c-5397-9871-6128556fb45a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2x}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-{e}^{-x}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{13}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919/selection/1c777339d49839348c4b5ebd3e039cabdf8ca6a6e549ea8f755772a7b6849fbf" :answer/id #uuid "d8ac31ca-0410-5fb5-b4b5-8854a1c1f2c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))}{9}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919/selection/f8756c165ec8ad0e568f58b1cd95dea8e4f5c948f1efe4753abff29aa1dcecf0" :answer/id #uuid "11656843-8c50-52ec-955b-59126c0105e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919/selection/4da407a7391a904c8d13803a6176a59a9ffaaad56fa9c03c8d9ca3ecdf148b33" :answer/id #uuid "8fb366fc-b818-5853-9694-2d87eba5f9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919/selection/b53c212a18c81f50996c61cac0be19d5888c5af3b2b02215623396d8d9de4d79" :answer/id #uuid "45a1bffd-81dd-56f8-883f-edeec8f59c3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce75557-f330-5e9d-b276-ab12594e1e61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12919/selection/f8756c165ec8ad0e568f58b1cd95dea8e4f5c948f1efe4753abff29aa1dcecf0" :answer-field/choices ["q-12919/selection/0f1b11f7d6616c0d1a0bcd0f9424e89602dea70c09ef29602c8cca57bf190eda" "q-12919/selection/1c777339d49839348c4b5ebd3e039cabdf8ca6a6e549ea8f755772a7b6849fbf" "q-12919/selection/f8756c165ec8ad0e568f58b1cd95dea8e4f5c948f1efe4753abff29aa1dcecf0" "q-12919/selection/4da407a7391a904c8d13803a6176a59a9ffaaad56fa9c03c8d9ca3ecdf148b33" "q-12919/selection/b53c212a18c81f50996c61cac0be19d5888c5af3b2b02215623396d8d9de4d79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12919" :question/id #uuid "34489983-3228-5451-8433-56868753d4c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-12919" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(-2{e}^{-2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{13}{9}I & =\\frac{3{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-2x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-12919/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b428331b-4916-5b2c-8aa6-89a2358cdef0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12919"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-14878"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{10}{9}I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{10}{9}I & =\\frac{3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{10}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-349030/field-1/933459efcc27c33c37c5b5ab8334bb7a1ed123e1c1fcd6368d829912b15d7948" :answer/id #uuid "1e2db65a-fc37-5636-a429-5d5db60c66e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e^{-4\\pi}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349030/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e9027a4-4ea8-508a-bfd3-4a0e2eddd4df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349030/field-1/933459efcc27c33c37c5b5ab8334bb7a1ed123e1c1fcd6368d829912b15d7948" :answer-field/choices ["q-349030/field-1/933459efcc27c33c37c5b5ab8334bb7a1ed123e1c1fcd6368d829912b15d7948"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349030" :question/id #uuid "6b48f842-2d47-5937-8d3e-e594261f9f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-349030" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{10}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by  $I=\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-4x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{-4x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{-4x})\\,(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))(-4{e}^{-4x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-4x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{-4x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{-4x})\\,(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))(-4{e}^{-4x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation for $I,$ we solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-4I \\\\ 5I & =-{e}^{-4x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{10}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(-\\frac{{e}^{-4x}}{10}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\frac{{e}^{-4\\pi }}{10}(0+1))-(-\\frac{1}{10}(0+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}-\\frac{{e}^{-4\\pi }}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(1-{e}^{-4\\pi }).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-349030/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1da25ef-5d1b-588f-b1cc-121562ff98ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349030"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348955/field-1/c3ff3fb17a8b26f7e0a22a76429b288be54509fc45ad98735e6e1741c95c3798" :answer/id #uuid "d9e8fccf-c196-54dc-88a9-2881afc199ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{3\\pi/2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348955/field-1/4c50d9016fd9489f5a6959e2adbf54b38af710c5ab60286790a7a149e0f29567" :answer/id #uuid "d89fc349-65b1-5765-ba47-5be3d2fd3e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{3\\pi/2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348955/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9180b05-50c3-55d8-84d4-6df068d68406" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348955/field-1/c3ff3fb17a8b26f7e0a22a76429b288be54509fc45ad98735e6e1741c95c3798" :answer-field/choices ["q-348955/field-1/c3ff3fb17a8b26f7e0a22a76429b288be54509fc45ad98735e6e1741c95c3798" "q-348955/field-1/4c50d9016fd9489f5a6959e2adbf54b38af710c5ab60286790a7a149e0f29567"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348955" :question/id #uuid "f59147ac-89e8-5b49-99ae-b5e4107f553c" :question/math-academy-id "q-348955" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{3}{13}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{3x})(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))(3{e}^{3x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{3}{2}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{3x})(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))(3{e}^{3x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3}{2}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{3}{2}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{3}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3}{2}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{9}{4}I \\\\ \\frac{13}{4}I & ={e}^{3x}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)) \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{13}{e}^{3x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{1}{13}{e}^{3x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{13}{e}^{3(\\pi /2)}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )))-(\\frac{1}{13}{e}^{3(0)}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}{e}^{3\\pi /2}(2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-1))-\\frac{3}{13} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{13}({e}^{3\\pi /2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348955/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1da25ef-5d1b-588f-b1cc-121562ff98ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348955"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012/selection/f7b89be140577d02205dc95e3958b2877ec0381709c446c645841b27833c6ce6" :answer/id #uuid "bf1a9da2-1578-59f7-8914-cb2658c2bf39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2\\pi }+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012/selection/c018dce262291d0618d02f356e48044d6babc3ad51a43a85916b07ed15e0bc7c" :answer/id #uuid "27f5778c-e151-5b58-9e42-a27103dbf21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}({e}^{2\\pi }+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012/selection/aa75ca17ba9ec3429f932ad814f24960d19aee75dd9656520d26e14edabffadf" :answer/id #uuid "db2f0f4b-6198-5752-9c20-e9f98205b990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{2\\pi }-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012/selection/bf690a6a442443070478445f2557a3acb5c99183bc15dc15e9c6049062d8dd3a" :answer/id #uuid "861c386c-8a73-5b67-9f6a-02555a852b80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-(2{e}^{2\\pi }+5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012/selection/d4b41616202d5c0b9d5c2e022494702a6db390a0b902a0092cb35101981f85fa" :answer/id #uuid "8f211399-e171-56f0-93e5-d10f3158739a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2\\pi }+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "02002b45-744b-5be3-bc93-56a680ffef79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83012/selection/c018dce262291d0618d02f356e48044d6babc3ad51a43a85916b07ed15e0bc7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-83012/selection/f7b89be140577d02205dc95e3958b2877ec0381709c446c645841b27833c6ce6" "q-83012/selection/c018dce262291d0618d02f356e48044d6babc3ad51a43a85916b07ed15e0bc7c" "q-83012/selection/aa75ca17ba9ec3429f932ad814f24960d19aee75dd9656520d26e14edabffadf" "q-83012/selection/bf690a6a442443070478445f2557a3acb5c99183bc15dc15e9c6049062d8dd3a" "q-83012/selection/d4b41616202d5c0b9d5c2e022494702a6db390a0b902a0092cb35101981f85fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83012" :question/id #uuid "db2f5081-4388-5d02-89b1-d05db7e0dc4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-83012" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2J \\\\ I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2(-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4I \\\\ 5I & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2\\pi }}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-\\frac{{e}^{2(0)}}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2{e}^{2\\pi }}{5}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}({e}^{2\\pi }+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83012/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1da25ef-5d1b-588f-b1cc-121562ff98ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83012"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967/selection/3385406d1a2673f87ca14f2e9cba70de5e39f176dc2b2d04d46897344cbae526" :answer/id #uuid "a55290bf-4acd-50db-a97a-451fe5e72f5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}({e}^{6\\pi }-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967/selection/f7f01f7332c554170358c613d774f468e4ce29608c342b5628fb32e94a893547" :answer/id #uuid "97af8afe-75c6-53bc-ab56-3a9c9e418456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10({e}^{6\\pi }-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967/selection/f503413ef962c94d1f6a162493c8416e551e90696ca6bf065996da37220cae7e" :answer/id #uuid "230c0e1c-c427-5c95-ac60-fb67a6b56cff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6\\pi }-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967/selection/ef66a6a45eac2180c7d21a2361afa175a8918f57425600bbe953849ef8b9f5c9" :answer/id #uuid "7f8ee124-605e-53e8-b56e-b6859bd07dd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}({e}^{6\\pi }+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967/selection/f7b89be140577d02205dc95e3958b2877ec0381709c446c645841b27833c6ce6" :answer/id #uuid "93ba6ba6-77f3-5e54-86c5-1426d51448d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2\\pi }+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b9391da-4dbb-5d79-b473-25c72a571962" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49967/selection/3385406d1a2673f87ca14f2e9cba70de5e39f176dc2b2d04d46897344cbae526" :answer-field/choices ["q-49967/selection/3385406d1a2673f87ca14f2e9cba70de5e39f176dc2b2d04d46897344cbae526" "q-49967/selection/f7f01f7332c554170358c613d774f468e4ce29608c342b5628fb32e94a893547" "q-49967/selection/f503413ef962c94d1f6a162493c8416e551e90696ca6bf065996da37220cae7e" "q-49967/selection/ef66a6a45eac2180c7d21a2361afa175a8918f57425600bbe953849ef8b9f5c9" "q-49967/selection/f7b89be140577d02205dc95e3958b2877ec0381709c446c645841b27833c6ce6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49967" :question/id #uuid "0f00816b-dc7a-5ff5-aa98-8c002fd0740e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49967" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(3{e}^{3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{3x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(3{e}^{3x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\int {e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3J \\\\ I & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3(-{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3I) \\\\ I & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-9I \\\\ 10I & ={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{3x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{10}){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2\\pi )}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi ))}{10}-\\frac{{e}^{3(0)}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{6\\pi }}{10}-\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}({e}^{6\\pi }-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49967/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1da25ef-5d1b-588f-b1cc-121562ff98ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49967"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362669/field-1/04451bd866a52ad02bf9d0e1ddb5f47932d0964ba3a0f6e4224d07a25d6c81b8" :answer/id #uuid "832df126-b4de-51d1-9f54-625406c82c5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{-\\pi}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362669/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "77e3ff65-9784-5471-a33f-a1ee5383e36f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362669/field-1/04451bd866a52ad02bf9d0e1ddb5f47932d0964ba3a0f6e4224d07a25d6c81b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-362669/field-1/04451bd866a52ad02bf9d0e1ddb5f47932d0964ba3a0f6e4224d07a25d6c81b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362669" :question/id #uuid "ae8972c6-41c0-5cb2-9053-0f9dfe222d7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-362669" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{10}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by  $I=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({e}^{-x})(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =({e}^{-x})(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))(-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation for $I,$ we solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}J \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{3}I) \\\\ I & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{9}I \\\\ 10I & ={e}^{-x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{10}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{10}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{10}(0-(-1)))-(\\frac{1}{10}(0-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{10}+\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}({e}^{-\\pi }+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-362669/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1da25ef-5d1b-588f-b1cc-121562ff98ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-497"] :question/worked-solution "First, we let\n\n$$\nI = \\int \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{3}⁡x-2\\int \\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={ln}^{3}⁡x-2I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $I,$ remembering to add a constant of integration $C$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={ln}^{3}⁡x-2I \\\\ 3I & ={ln}^{3}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡x}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-498"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int e^{x}\\sin{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ = \\int e^{x}\\cos{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula once more, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-I \\\\ 2I & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7313"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/2} e^x\\sin(2x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I = \\displaystyle \\int e^{x}\\sin(2x)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ = \\int e^{x}\\cos(2x)\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula once more, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})({e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting this into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I\\mathbin.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}I \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}{5}){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}))}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{\\pi /2}}{5}+\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}({e}^{\\pi /2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
